# pip's vendored bundle: msgpack 1.1.2 and setuptools/pkg_resources 70.3.0.
#
#   GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964  msgpack     OOB read on Unpacker reuse
#   CVE-2025-47273       setuptools  path traversal in PackageIndex
#
# These are pip's own frozen copies under site-packages/pip/_vendor/, not
# packages Hermes imports (confirmed by reading the built image: the vendored
# msgpack/__init__.py declares version (1, 1, 2), with pkg_resources beside it).
# Trivy files them under its aggregate "Python" target with no path in the
# report summary and no "(METADATA)" marker -- that missing marker is the tell.
#
# Not fixable: the versions are frozen inside pip. Removing pip is unsafe
# because Hermes lazy-installs skill dependencies at runtime. Both are only
# reachable through pip's own index traffic, which this container cannot
# originate -- internal=true network, no direct egress, all tools via Trentina.
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964
CVE-2025-47273

# NOTE: the PyJWT, Starlette and MCP SDK entries that used to live here are
# gone on purpose. Hermes 0.21.0 ships PyJWT 2.13.0, starlette 1.3.1 and
# mcp 2.0.0, all of which carry the fixes. Building from upstream's lockfile
# retired them rather than suppressing them.
